#4582 This PR marks renamed exports in the docs app and removes duplicate pages. For example `flatMap` doc is now not a separate page and is also removed from https://rxjs.dev/api/operators. It's just mentioned on https://rxjs.dev/api/operators/mergeMap as an alias for `mergeMap`.

@JWO719 At the end I didn't even have to use `typescript` as I wanted here https://github.com/ReactiveX/rxjs/issues/4582#issuecomment-472821147 because everything is already parsed by `dgeni-packages` typescript processor, it's just not mentioned anywhere https://github.com/angular/dgeni-packages/blob/master/typescript/src/processors/readTypeScriptModules/index.ts#L95-L99.
Also I wrote this processor in TypeScript and then updated `package.json` scripts with `ts-node` because it already works nicely without any other changes with the existing JavaScript codebase. I can eventually rewrite it to JavaScript like the rest of the code.

This is an addition to #4879. I've noticed there's some forgotten [`/spec/operators/forkJoin-spec.ts`](https://github.com/ReactiveX/rxjs/blob/master/spec/operators/forkJoin-spec.ts) that was overriding the marble diagram from the correct `forkJoin` spec here [`/spec/observables/forkJoin-spec.ts`](https://github.com/ReactiveX/rxjs/blob/master/spec/observables/forkJoin-spec.ts). But the old diagram is probably more descriptive (this is the one use at https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/forkJoin right now):

```
  asDiagram('forkJoin')('should emit the last emitted value from each observable', () => {
    const e1 =   hot('-a--b-----c-d-e-|');
    const e2 =   cold('--1--2-3-4---|   ');
    const e3 =   hot('--------f--g-h-i--j-|');
    const expected = '--------------------(z|)';
    const expectedValue = {
      z: ['e', '4', 'j']
    };
    const result = forkJoin(e1, e2, e3);
    expectObservable(result).toBe(expected, expectedValue);
  });
```

So I pasted this initial test over the current one in [`/spec/observables/forkJoin-spec.ts`](https://github.com/ReactiveX/rxjs/blob/master/spec/observables/forkJoin-spec.ts) and just switched the order of source Observables because "hot" Observable as always listed first so the marble diagram will match the code. https://github.com/ReactiveX/rxjs/blob/master/spec/helpers/tests2png/diagram-test-runner.ts#L15

Related issue (if exists): #4879

- Also adds tests and test harness for requestAnimationFrame stubbing with sinon
- Updates TypeScript lib to use ES2018 (so we can use `findIndex` on `Array`).

## This is a proposed API, we haven't decided on anything yet

Example 1: Just a simple use.
```ts
import { animationFrames } from 'rxjs';

// Log the elapsed milliseconds at each animation frame.
animationFrames().subscribe(elapsed => console.log(elapsed));
```

Example 2: Tweening animation function
```ts
 import { animationFrames } from 'rxjs';
 import { map, takeWhile, endWith } from 'rxjs/operators';
 
 function tween(start: number, end: number, duration: number) {
   const diff = end - start;
   return animationFrames().pipe(
     // Figure out what percentage of time has passed
     map(elapsed => elapsed / duration),
     // Take the vector while less than 100%
     takeWhile(v => v < 1),
     // Finish with 100%
     endWith(1),
     // Calculate the distance traveled between start and end
     map(v => v * diff + start)
   );
 }
 
 // Setup a div for us to move around
 const div = document.createElement('div');
 document.body.appendChild(div);
 div.style.position = 'absolute';
 div.style.width = '40px';
 div.style.height = '40px';
 div.style.backgroundColor = 'lime';
 div.style.transform = 'translate3d(10px, 0, 0)';
 
 tween(10, 200, 4000).subscribe(x => {
   div.style.transform = `translate3d(${x}px, 0, 0)`;
 });
```

See documentation in code for more information.

### Highlights:

- Starts a single animation loop for N subscriptions.
- If no more subscribers are subscribed to the animation loop, it will terminate the animation loop.
- Replacement for odd patterns like `range(0, animationFrameScheduler)` or `interval(0, animationFrameScheduler)`
- Outputs more useful values for animations than above recipes.

### TBD:

- Do we want this at all?
- Do we want to export this from `rxjs`, or do we add a new import site for `rxjs/animation`?  If the latter, does it need to be `dom-animation`?
- Recommendations for testing usage of this to be included in docs? 
- Do we find this approach agreeable? 
  - Is `Observable<void>` preferrable, and make users compose to get the elapsed time? 
  - Do we keep it as-is?
  - Do we want each subscription to this to start a different animation loop? (Seems inefficient)
